hostCall is operation
hostCall purpose "Run a host target for compiled code: the key's shape, then its target with the call's slots; gives 0 or an error's variant number, its payload stored: refined_host"
hostCall invariant runsTargets "\"Each target behaves as its handler in host.py and the C runtime do, its error variants and traps included\""
hostCall typeParameter none
hostCall input key machine.Address copied
hostCall input bytes Int64 copied
hostCall input args machine.Address copied
hostCall input results machine.Address copied
hostCall input payload machine.Address copied
hostCall output Int32
hostCall outputOwnedBy none
hostCall raises none
hostCall effect use machine.memory
hostCall effect use system.calls
hostCall uses memoryAccess
hostCall uses systemCalls
hostCall memoryHeap false
hostCall async false
hostCall maxRecursion none
hostCall abi c "refined_host"
hostCall label begin loopKind none
hostCall label begin within none
hostCall label readRowDone loopKind none
hostCall label readRowDone within none
hostCall label checkScope loopKind none
hostCall label checkScope within none
hostCall label run loopKind none
hostCall label run within none
hostCall let zero Int64 0 immutable
hostCall let sixteen Int64 16 immutable
hostCall let twentyFour Int64 24 immutable
hostCall let one Int64 1 immutable
hostCall at begin do findShape
hostCall at begin do clearPayload
hostCall at begin do readNumber
hostCall at begin do readRow
hostCall at begin branch ifError readRow goto run else goto readRowDone
hostCall at readRowDone do readScoped
hostCall at readRowDone do scopedCheck
hostCall at readRowDone branch if isScoped goto checkScope else goto run
hostCall at checkScope do readName
